---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EvalExample from '../../components/EvalExample.astro';
import { examples, method, taxonomy } from '../../data/evaluations';
import { roles, RESUME } from '../../data/experience';

const aiRoles = roles.filter((r) => r.area === 'AI evaluation');
---
<Base title="AI Evaluation" description="How Kolawole Odewusi evaluates AI output: a five-step method, an error taxonomy and three worked examples checked against public datasets.">
  <article>
    <header class="wrap head">
      <p class="eyebrow">AI evaluation</p>
      <h1>How I evaluate AI output</h1>
      <p class="lede">Fluent answers can still be wrong. My work is finding where: checking a response against its instructions and its sources, naming each error, and writing down the evidence so the judgement can be reviewed.</p>
      <aside class="about" aria-label="About the examples on this page">
        <p><strong>About the examples.</strong> The three examples below are illustrative, written for this portfolio. Their prompts and responses are invented, but every judgement is checked against the public, fictional datasets in my case studies, so you can verify each one. None of this comes from employer or client work, which stays confidential.</p>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <section class="wrap sec" aria-labelledby="where-h">
      <h2 id="where-h">Where I've done this work</h2>
      <ul class="roles">
        {aiRoles.map((r) => <li><span class="mono when">{r.when}</span> <strong>{r.title}</strong> <span class="muted">· {r.org}</span></li>)}
      </ul>
      <p class="small muted">Evaluating LLM output for factual correctness, hallucinations and logical consistency against rubrics; designing adversarial tasks; and reviewing video and robotics training data against quality guidelines. Details are in the <a href="/#experience">experience timeline</a> and <a href={RESUME} type="application/pdf">resume</a>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap sec" aria-labelledby="method-h">
      <h2 id="method-h">The method</h2>
      <ol class="method">
        {method.map((m, i) => (
          <li>
            <span class="num mono">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <h3>{m.step}</h3>
            <p>{m.detail}</p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap sec" aria-labelledby="tax-h">
      <h2 id="tax-h">What I look for</h2>
      <p class="muted">Six error types, each with a severity. Naming the type makes issues comparable across responses and reviewers.</p>
      <dl class="tax">
        {taxonomy.map((t) => <div><dt>{t.type}</dt><dd>{t.what}</dd></div>)}
      </dl>
    </section>

    <section class="wrap sec" aria-labelledby="ex-h">
      <h2 id="ex-h">Worked examples</h2>
      <p class="muted">Each example shows the prompt, the response with my notes, a five-criterion rubric, a verdict and a corrected answer. Use the button to read a response without the notes first.</p>
      {examples.map((ex, i) => <EvalExample example={ex} index={i + 1} />)}
    </section>

    <section class="wrap sec end" aria-labelledby="next-h">
      <h2 id="next-h">The same habit, applied to analysis</h2>
      <p>My <a href="/work/">case studies</a> apply the same discipline to data work: figures traced to their source, rates checked against their denominators, and recommendations kept separate from what the data can show.</p>
      <p><a class="btn btn--primary" href="/#contact">Get in touch</a> <a class="btn" href={RESUME} type="application/pdf">View my resume</a></p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .head { padding-block: var(--s-8) var(--s-5); }
  .head h1 { max-width: 16ch; }
  .about { border-left: 2px solid var(--cobalt-mark); padding: var(--s-1) 0 var(--s-1) var(--s-4); margin-top: var(--s-5); max-width: var(--measure); font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--ink-2); }
  .about p { margin: 0; }
  .sec { padding-block: var(--s-7); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
  .sec > p, .sec > h2 { max-width: 46rem; }
  .roles { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0 0 var(--s-4); max-width: none; border-top: 1px solid var(--ink); }
  .roles li { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--s-2) var(--s-4); align-items: baseline; padding: var(--s-3) 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); margin: 0; }
  .when { font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--ink-2); min-width: 10rem; }
  .method { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--s-5); max-width: none; }
  .method li { margin: 0; border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-top: var(--s-3); }
  .method .num { color: var(--cobalt); font-size: var(--step--1); }
  .method h3 { margin: var(--s-2) 0; font-size: var(--step-0); }
  .method p { font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--ink-2); margin: 0; }
  .tax { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: var(--s-4) var(--s-6); margin: var(--s-4) 0 0; }
  .tax div { border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-top: var(--s-3); }
  .tax dt { font-weight: 600; }
  .tax dd { margin: var(--s-1) 0 0; font-size: var(--step--1); color: var(--ink-2); }
  .end .btn { margin: var(--s-2) var(--s-2) 0 0; }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) { .method { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } .tax { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .method, .tax { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
